.TH "MUTATIONRECORD.NEXTSIBLING" "3JS" "October 21, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MutationRecord.nextSibling \- MutationRecord: nextSibling property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[CR]MutationRecord\f[R] read\-only property
\f[B]\f[CB]nextSibling\f[B]\f[R] is the next sibling of an added or
removed child node of the \f[CR]target\f[R] of a
\f[CR]MutationObserver\f[R].
.SH VALUE
If a node is added to or removed from the \f[CR]target\f[R] of a
\f[CR]MutationObserver\f[R], the value is the \f[CR]Node\f[R] that is
the next sibling of the added or removed node: that is, the node
immediately following this one in the parent\(cqs \f[CR]childNodes\f[R]
list.
.PP
The value is \f[CR]null\f[R] if there are no added or removed nodes, or
if the node is the last child of its parent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Log the next sibling of a mutation
This adds/removes a node every time you click the button, but it
performs the update at the \f[I]start of the target\f[R], not the end.
Then the observer logs the \f[CR]textContent\f[R] of the
\f[CR]nextSibling\f[R] of the updated node.
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqadd\-nodes\(dq>Add a node</\f[B]button\f[R]>
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqremove\-nodes\(dq>Remove a node</\f[B]button\f[R]>
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqreset\(dq>Reset</\f[B]button\f[R]>

<\f[B]pre\f[R] id=\(dqlog\(dq class=\(dqlog\(dq>Next sibling of updated node:</\f[B]pre\f[R]>
<\f[B]div\f[R] id=\(dqtarget\(dq><\f[B]p\f[R]>Node #0</\f[B]p\f[R]></\f[B]div\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] addNodes = document.querySelector(\(dq#add\-nodes\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] removeNodes = document.querySelector(\(dq#remove\-nodes\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] reset = document.querySelector(\(dq#reset\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] target = document.querySelector(\(dq#target\(dq);

addNodes.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] newPara = document.createElement(\(dqp\(dq);
  newPara.textContent = \(gaNode #${target.childElementCount}\(ga;
  target.insertBefore(newPara, target.firstChild);
});

removeNodes.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] oldPara = target.firstChild;
  \f[B]if\f[R] (oldPara) {
    target.removeChild(oldPara);
  }
});

reset.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] self.location.reload());

\f[B]function\f[R] logNextSibling(records) {
  \f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] record \f[B]of\f[R] records) {
    \f[B]if\f[R] (record.type === \(dqchildList\(dq) {
      log.textContent = \(gaNext sibling of updated node: ${record.nextSibling?.textContent ?? \f[B]null\f[R]}\(ga;
    }
  }
}

\f[B]const\f[R] observer = \f[B]new\f[R] MutationObserver(logNextSibling);
observer.observe(target, { childList: \f[B]true\f[R] });
.EE
.SS Result
